--[[
	Anomaly Coop - NPC group (W4 "npc"): companions for every player (SPEC R-4.3).
	Port of the behaviour of xrRazom 1.4 xrr_patch_companions, extended: a client's companion follows that
	client, not the host (xrRazom put every companion in the host's squad).

	Companions are squads in the host's ALife (axr_companions). A client's dialog runs on the client, where
	the squads are frozen copies, so:
	Client: the companion dialog actions (recruit, dismiss, every order: wait/follow, stealth, combat type,
	  distance, patrol, waypoints, looting) are not run locally; they go to the host (npc.comp).
	Host: runs the stock action for that player: the player becomes the squad's leader; waypoint orders run
	  with "the actor" = the player's proxy (dropped where that player stands). While a companion of a client thinks (axr_beh), "actor" in its logic is that client's
	  proxy: it follows, covers and keeps distance to its own player. The leader is saved with the game.
	  The NPC flags the dialogs read (npcx_is_companion, npcx_beh_*) are mirrored to every player (npc.comp_info): a companion
	  is the group's. Every player gives it orders and uses its inventory (owner 2026-11-01); control says whom it follows.
	Recruit (Ruling F2-34, F2 T12 round 2): the host takes it only if that player held the talk lock of the NPC, or of
	  another member of its squad, now or in the last 5 s (coop.talk_recent). The stock recruit conditions live in the
	  dialog, which runs on the client; without a talk a modified client could recruit any free squad in 15 m and
	  open its inventory (F2-32b: one's own companion's inventory needs no talk). 5 s and not "holds now": the host
	  applies the DialogUnlock of the closing talk window in the session update, before the npc.comp event reaches Lua.
	Companions a task gives (setup_companion_task, add_task_companion, add_speaker_companion, add_special_squad,
	  nta_utils.spawn_companion_squad) join the player the task was taken by (coop_tasks.reward_peer): the squads such
	  a call adds are led by his proxy. add_speaker_companion takes the giver of the request for the speaker (the host
	  is not talking while a client takes the task).
	Control (owner's request 2026-11-01): a companion squad follows one leader, a player. Only he dismisses it (dm_companion_leave,
	  any other player gets refused, with the reason; the same action in a story's dialog, the Fanatic's training, is anybody's in a talk with it, and the
	  story's next recruit gives the companion back to who led it), the other orders are everybody's. The leader hands it to another
	  player (a line of the companion's list of commands, then a line per player; a character with no such list, the Fanatic, has the
	  dialog dm_coop_companion_hand), any other player takes it (the dialog dm_coop_companion_take, modxml_coop_companions). The host
	  decides (host_lead, its own dialog takes the same path): the asker must be a player of the session, the NPC a living companion
	  within 15 m, and only the leader hands over. Control passes between players of one level (owner 2026-11-02): a player of another
	  level stays in the list, says so, and the process that leads the level refuses by the engine's table (coop.levels.level_of_player);
	  a story's NPC of a task the same.
	  Both players get a short message. leaders[] holds the character (a proxy id, which a character keeps in the save); a
	  squad with no entry is the host's. A line of npc.comp_info says who leads it. The answer takes a round trip and the
	  talk window reads the conditions at once, so a line just used stays away for TAKE_WAIT_MS.
	A leader who leaves: his entry stays, saved with the game; while his character is out of the world the squad acts for
	  the host (control_peer, leader_of). It is his again when he comes back, unless somebody took it meanwhile. Chosen over
	  "passes to the host for good": nobody finds his companions gone after a reconnect, and over "waits for him": the group
	  is not left with idle companions.
	Every "the actor" of a companion is its leader:
	  axr_beh and the combat of Useful Idiots run with_identity; Useful Idiots' follower list is per leader (formations);
	  who is an enemy (on_enemy_eval) is judged for the leader; offline travel: get_current_task of a squad that goes to
	  "the actor" (target 0, the stock's scripted_target) goes to the leader instead, and Useful Idiots' offline rule stays;
	  the keys, the wheel, the panel and the squad list of the host cover the squads he leads (filtered companion_squads,
	  own_squads_only); a client's orders reach his companions at any distance; a client's go-to key: npc.comp_go.
	  A group's level change: nothing to do. The stock on_level_changing puts the squads at the group's arrival, and the engine
	  puts every mover's character there too (host_place_movers), a late one next to the host (bring_proxy_to_level).
	  Inventory: one backpack for the group. The host's stock table is the truth, a client's moves go there (npc.comp_item), the
	  list goes to every player (npc.comp_items), so what one gave another can take; F2-32b reads is_group_companion.
	Split levels (docs\SPLIT_LEVELS.md 7a): leaders[] and the stock's table are the business of the process that leads the squad's level.
	  A map server's actor is a ghost: a companion with no leader here goes to the nearest player (follows). Its leaders go up into the
	  world server's save and down onto a new map server (coop_levels_share). A squad claimed by a task on a map server's level goes there
	  (npc.comp_adopt, with the stock's marks, which the world server writes itself where the stock has no live NPC to write them on, and the
	  logic of a companion). The host's level change takes only his own squads
	  (companion_squad_can_teleport). A leader who goes to another level: the authority lets the squad go, the world server teleports it
	  to his body when nothing of it is online at a map server, the level of arrival adopts it (a map server keeps its owner until the
	  world server took it, npc.comp_drop with m; the save keeps the owner of a squad on its way); a squad the stock forbids to teleport
	  (told to wait, the Fanatic) stays and keeps its leader's entry. A map server does this with nobody left on its level too; the world
	  server stands in for a level nobody leads (a level entered together leaves a squad behind while its leader comes along).
	A client's "my companions" (list_actor_squad_by_id, NPC.getCompanions) are the NPCs npc.comp_info says he controls: the stock table
	  is empty or false there. Not covered: the stock's panel on a client (activate_hud is an axr_companions callback, host), the
	  orders of Useful Idiots' wheel and keys on a client (this file forwards none of them), unstuck()'s distance to the host, the overweight
	  gate on a client.

	Events (ids in host numbering):
	  npc.comp       client -> host  { f = "module.function", i = npc, d = dialog id }
	  npc.comp_info  host -> client  { i = npc, s = "flag1,flag2,...", l = peer who holds control, nil: nobody's companion }
	  npc.comp_lead  client -> host  { a = "take" | "give", i = npc, to = peer }
	  npc.comp_msg   host -> client  { k = string id, n = NPC's name, w = player's nick, a = peer whose nick n is, on the reader's machine }
	  npc.comp_talk  host -> client  { i = npc, b = allow break }: force_talk of a companion's logic, on its leader's machine
	  npc.comp_follow map server -> world server  { s = squad, p = leader's peer, l = his character }: his squad is let go
	  npc.comp_adopt world server -> map server   { s = squad, l = character, p = peer, d, c = the stock's marks: no dismiss, no teleport }
	  npc.comp_drop  world server -> map server   { s = squad, m = true: it went to its leader, forget it without a dismissal }: a task let it go
	  npc.comp_recall world server -> map server  { s = squad }: a squad it let go (comp_follow) is held online by a friend: offline now
	  npc.comp_req   client -> host  {}: his Lua state is new, send everything
	  npc.comp_go    client -> host  { x, y, z }: his companions go there
	  npc.comp_item  client -> host  { i = npc, o = item, g = true: gave, false: took }
	  npc.comp_items host -> client  { i = npc, s = "id,id,...": what the group may take back }
	Stock functions wrapped: dialogs_axr_companion.<the actions below>, is_not_actor_companion,
	dm_init_is_actor_companion, dialogs_lostzone and dialogs_agr_u companion setters (if present),
	axr_beh.action_beh.execute, sim_squad_scripted:get_current_task, axr_companions.cycle_state, move_to_point,
	list_actor_squad_by_id, get_nearby_companion, is_assigned_item, is_assigned_companion, transfer_item, companion_squad_can_teleport,
dismiss_special_squad; xr_effects.force_talk; of Useful Idiots
	NPC.getCompanions, getTargetCompanion, the surge patch's companion helpers, onEvalEnemy, its combat actions.
--]]

local tostring, tonumber, type, pairs, ipairs, pcall, next = tostring, tonumber, type, pairs, ipairs, pcall, next

local TAG = "companions"
local P -- coop_npc_players

local function log(fmt, ...) P.log(TAG, fmt, ...) end
local function report(what, err) P.report(TAG, what, err) end

local EV_CMD, EV_INFO = "npc.comp", "npc.comp_info"
local EV_LEAD, EV_MSG, EV_REQ, EV_GO = "npc.comp_lead", "npc.comp_msg", "npc.comp_req", "npc.comp_go"
local EV_ITEM, EV_ITEMS = "npc.comp_item", "npc.comp_items"
local EV_FOLLOW, EV_ADOPT, EV_TALK, EV_DROP = "npc.comp_follow", "npc.comp_adopt", "npc.comp_talk", "npc.comp_drop"
-- world server -> map server: a squad it let go is held online there by a friend: take it offline now (on_recall). RECALLED: `leaving` of
-- such a squad on the map server; RECALL_AGAIN_MS: the world server asks again after this long if it still did not come home
local EV_RECALL, RECALLED, RECALL_AGAIN_MS = "npc.comp_recall", "recalled", 20000

-- Dialog actions forwarded to the host. Value: "add" / "remove" changes the leader, true = an order.
local ACTIONS = {
	["dialogs_axr_companion.become_actor_companion"] = "add",
	["dialogs_axr_companion.remove_companions_from_squad"] = "remove",
	["dialogs_lostzone.set_stalker_living_legend_as_companion"] = "add",
	["dialogs_lostzone.set_degtyarev_taskforce_squad_as_companion"] = "add",
	["dialogs_lostzone.dismiss_speaker_companion"] = "remove",
	["dialogs_agr_u.set_speaker_as_companion"] = "add",
	["dialogs_escape.set_esc_2_12_stalker_fanat_as_companion"] = "add",
	-- a hire: the stock contract table is read by the host's timer, the days the client paid come with the order (paid_period)
	["txr_paid_companions.register_paid_companion"] = true,
}
local PAID = "txr_paid_companions.register_paid_companion"
local LEAVE_DIALOG = "dm_companion_leave" -- the stock menu's "leave me": the leader's. The same action in a story's dialog is anybody's.
local PAID_SECONDS = { take_guard_money_1 = 86400, take_guard_money_2 = 172800 } -- the stock's guard_period, a file local
for _, n in ipairs({
	"set_companion_to_stealth_substate", "set_companion_to_default_substate", "set_companion_to_wait_state",
	"set_companion_to_follow_state", "set_companion_to_attack_state", "set_companion_to_ignore_combat_state",
	"set_companion_to_attack_only_actor_combat_enemy_state", "switch_companion_distance",
	"set_companion_hide_in_cover", "set_companion_combat_type_camper", "set_companion_combat_type_monolith",
	"set_companion_combat_type_default", "switch_companion_patrol_mode", "companion_add_waypoints",
	"companion_remove_waypoints", "switch_companion_gather_items", "switch_companion_loot_corpses",
}) do
	ACTIONS["dialogs_axr_companion." .. n] = true
end

-- Orders that use db.actor's position (stock: waypoints are dropped where the player stands).
local POSITIONAL = { ["dialogs_axr_companion.companion_add_waypoints"] = true }

-- NPC info portions the companion dialogs read.
local FLAGS = {
	"npcx_is_companion", "npcx_beh_cannot_dismiss", "npcx_beh_substate_stealth", "npcx_beh_ignore_combat",
	"npcx_beh_ignore_actor_enemies", "npcx_beh_wait", "npcx_beh_distance_far", "npcx_beh_hide_in_cover",
	"npcx_beh_combat_tactics_camper", "npcx_beh_combat_tactics_monolith", "npcx_beh_patrol_mode",
	"npcx_beh_gather_items", "npcx_beh_loot_corpses",
}

local installed = false
local host_on = false
local orig = {}
local leaders = {} -- host: squad id -> proxy id (host numbering) of the client that leads it
local far = {} -- world server: level id -> { squad id -> proxy id }: what the map servers lead, for the save (coop_levels_share)
local last_leader = {} -- host: squad id -> who led it when a story's line let it go (0: the world server's player): he gets it back
local far_last = {} -- world server: level id -> last_leader of that map server, for the save
local down_heard = false -- map server: it took the leaders of its level from the world server
local sort_due = false -- the leaders came from a save: those of the other levels are to be sorted out
local view = {} -- client: NPC id -> peer who holds control of it (npc.comp_info)
local waiting_flags = {} -- client: NPC id -> flags that came while the NPC was not here
local visible = {} -- client: NPC id -> { item id = true }: what the leader may take back (npc.comp_items)
local asked = false -- client: this Lua state asked the host for everything (npc.comp_req)
local every_companion = 0 -- host: > 0 while Useful Idiots' surge code runs: it needs every companion, whoever leads
local stats = { cmd_out = 0, cmd_in = 0, refused = 0, refused_talk = 0, info_out = 0, info_in = 0, follow = 0, task_squads = 0,
	lead = 0, lead_refused = 0, go = 0, recall = 0 }
local RECRUIT_TALK_MS = 5000 -- Ruling F2-34: a recruit within this long after a talk with the squad
local FACE_TO_FACE_SQR = 225 -- 15 m: the dialog was face to face
local OTHER_PLAYERS = 7 -- lines of the choice of player: a full session less the asker (peers 0..7)
local PHRASE_HAND, PHRASE_WHOM, PHRASE_BACK, PHRASE_SLOTS = 7000, 7001, 7002, 7010 -- free ids of dm_is_actor_companion_dialog
local PHRASE_GOODWILL = -10001 -- the engine sorts by this: after the stock lines (-10000)
local paid_period = nil -- client: the seconds of the contract he just paid for
local TAKE_WAIT_MS = 3000 -- a line of control just used stays away this long, the host's answer is on its way
local asked_lead = {} -- NPC id -> time_global() of this machine's last request about its control
local lead_peer = {} -- squad id -> its leader's peer, while this process knows him
local refuse_dismiss -- host: its own dismiss of a companion somebody else leads (set below, it needs lead_for)
local claimed_far -- world server: a squad just claimed on a map server's level goes there (set below, it needs adopt)
local mark_far -- world server: the stock's marks of a task's squad on a map server's level (set below, it needs map_server_of)
local note_let_go, give_back -- a story's dismissal and its next recruit (set below, they need control_peer, squad_ids)
local teleport_rule -- axr_companions.companion_squad_can_teleport as this script wrapped it

local function resolve(full)
	local mod, fn = full:match("^([%w_]+)%.([%w_]+)$")
	local m = mod and _G[mod]
	return m, fn
end

local function squad_of(npc)
	local ok, sq = pcall(get_object_squad, npc)
	return ok and sq or nil
end

-- The stock's own test: a loaded squad is false until its first update.
local function is_companion_squad(squad)
	return not not squad and axr_companions ~= nil and axr_companions.companion_squads[squad.id] ~= nil
end

-- The NPC of a stock (actor, npc) pair, in either order.
local function npc_of(a, b)
	if a and a:id() ~= 0 then return a end
	return b
end

local function nick_of(peer)
	for _, p in ipairs(P.players()) do
		if p.id == peer then return tostring(p.nick) end
	end
	return "?"
end

-- The other players in the world, in the order of the choice of player. One of another level stays in the list.
local function other_players()
	local list = {}
	for _, p in ipairs(P.players()) do
		if not p.is_self and (type(p.avatar_id) == "number" or p.elsewhere == true) then list[#list + 1] = p end
	end
	return list
end

local function split_levels()
	local api = rawget(_G, "coop")
	local l = api and api.levels
	return l and l.split and l.split() == true and l or nil
end

-- The level a squad stands on: its id and its name; nil when this process cannot tell.
local function level_of_squad(squad)
	local ok, id, name = pcall(function()
		local lid = game_graph():vertex(squad.m_game_vertex_id):level_id()
		return lid, alife():level_name(lid)
	end)
	if ok then return id, name end
	return nil
end

local function far_leader(squad_id)
	for _, row in pairs(far) do
		if row[squad_id] then return row[squad_id] end
	end
	return nil
end

-- World server: whose word this squad is now; level_id nil: no map server's.
local function note_far(level_id, squad_id, lead)
	for _, row in pairs(far) do row[squad_id] = nil end
	if level_id == nil then return end
	far[level_id] = far[level_id] or {}
	far[level_id][squad_id] = lead
end

-- Do these two stand on different levels? The engine's table says, on the process that leads the level: no client decides this.
local function on_other_level(a, b)
	local l = split_levels()
	if not l then return false end
	local la, lb = l.level_of_player(a), l.level_of_player(b)
	return la ~= nil and lb ~= nil and la ~= lb
end

local function idiots_lib(name)
	local t = type(package) == "table" and package.loaded and package.loaded[name]
	return type(t) == "table" and t or nil
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Client: dialog actions go to the host
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function patch_client_actions()
	for full in pairs(ACTIONS) do
		local m, fn = resolve(full)
		local f = m and m[fn]
		if type(f) == "function" and not orig[full] then
			orig[full] = f
			m[fn] = function(a, b, dialog_id, ...)
				local npc = (a and a:id() == 0) and b or a
				if not P.client_live() then
					local kind = ACTIONS[full]
					if kind == "remove" then
						if refuse_dismiss(npc, dialog_id) then return end
						note_let_go(squad_of(npc), dialog_id)
					end
					if kind ~= "add" then return f(a, b, dialog_id, ...) end
					local before = squads_now()
					local res = f(a, b, dialog_id, ...)
					give_back(before)
					return res
				end
				if npc and P.send(EV_CMD, { f = full, i = P.to_host(npc:id()), p = paid_period, d = dialog_id }, 0) then
					stats.cmd_out = stats.cmd_out + 1
				end
			end
		end
	end
	local paid = _G["txr_paid_companions"]
	for fn, seconds in pairs(PAID_SECONDS) do
		local f = paid and paid[fn]
		if type(f) == "function" then
			paid[fn] = function(...)
				paid_period = seconds
				return f(...)
			end
		end
	end
end

local function apply_flags(npc, s)
	local on = {}
	for flag in s:gmatch("[%w_]+") do on[flag] = true end
	for _, flag in ipairs(FLAGS) do
		local has = npc:has_info(flag)
		if on[flag] and not has then
			npc:give_info_portion(flag)
		elseif not on[flag] and has then
			npc:disable_info_portion(flag)
		end
	end
end

local function client_on_info(t)
	if type(t.i) ~= "number" or type(t.s) ~= "string" then return end
	local id = P.to_local(t.i)
	view[id] = type(t.l) == "number" and t.l or nil
	if view[id] == nil then visible[id] = nil end
	stats.info_in = stats.info_in + 1
	local npc = level.object_by_id(id)
	if npc then
		waiting_flags[id] = nil
		apply_flags(npc, t.s)
	else
		waiting_flags[id] = t.s -- not online here yet: the host says it once
	end
end

-- Client: the NPCs of the squads this player leads, by the authority's word (npc.comp_info). The stock table is no help here: its rows
-- are false after a load until squad_on_first_update, a host-domain callback, and a recruit writes it on the authority only.
local function client_own_ids()
	local me, ids = P.self_peer(), {}
	for id, peer in pairs(view) do
		if peer == me then ids[#ids + 1] = id end
	end
	table.sort(ids)
	return ids
end

local function client_on_items(t)
	if type(t.i) ~= "number" or type(t.s) ~= "string" then return end
	local set = {}
	for id in t.s:gmatch("%d+") do set[P.to_local(tonumber(id))] = true end
	visible[P.to_local(t.i)] = set
end

-- A short message: in the talk window while a talk is on (it covers the HUD), on the HUD otherwise.
local function show(key, name, nick)
	local text = game.translate_string(key)
	local ok, line = pcall(string.format, text, tostring(name or ""), tostring(nick or ""))
	line = ok and line or text
	local a = db.actor
	if a and a:is_talking() then
		a:give_talk_message2(game.translate_string("st_coop_comp_caption"), line, "ui_iconsTotal_grouping", "iconed_answer_item")
	else
		actor_menu.set_msg(1, line, 8)
	end
end

local function client_on_msg(t)
	if type(t.k) == "string" then show(t.k, type(t.a) == "number" and nick_of(t.a) or t.n, t.w) end
end

-- Client: the item list the host sent, and what he did since (ui_inventory's move reports it, a talk's take-all goes
-- through transfer_item). The stock table of this machine stays empty: its writers are host-domain callbacks.
local function note_item(npc_id, item_id, gave)
	local set = visible[npc_id] or {}
	visible[npc_id] = set
	set[item_id] = gave and true or nil
	P.send(EV_ITEM, { i = P.to_host(npc_id), o = P.to_host(item_id), g = gave }, 0)
end

local function on_item_after_move(npc_id, obj, mode, bag_from)
	if not (mode == "loot" and P.client_live() and view[npc_id] ~= nil) then return end
	if bag_from == EDDListType.iActorBag then
		note_item(npc_id, obj:id(), true)
	elseif bag_from == EDDListType.iDeadBodyBag then
		note_item(npc_id, obj:id(), false)
	end
end

local function patch_items()
	local ac = axr_companions
	if not ac then return end
	local assigned, companion, transfer = ac.is_assigned_item, ac.is_assigned_companion, ac.transfer_item
	if type(assigned) == "function" then
		ac.is_assigned_item = function(npc_id, item_id)
			local set = visible[npc_id]
			if set and set[item_id] then return true end
			return assigned(npc_id, item_id)
		end
	end
	if type(companion) == "function" then
		ac.is_assigned_companion = function(a, b)
			local npc = npc_of(a, b)
			local set = npc and visible[npc:id()]
			if set and next(set) ~= nil then return true end
			return companion(a, b)
		end
	end
	if type(transfer) == "function" then
		ac.transfer_item = function(item_id, from, to, no_snd)
			local take = from and from:id() ~= 0
			local npc_id = take and from:id() or (to and to:id())
			local set = npc_id and visible[npc_id]
			if not (P.client_live() and to and npc_id and view[npc_id] ~= nil and (not take or (set and set[item_id]))) then
				return transfer(item_id, from, to, no_snd)
			end
			local item = level.object_by_id(item_id)
			if not item then return end
			from:transfer_item(item, to)
			note_item(npc_id, item_id, not take)
			if not no_snd then itms_manager.play_item_sound(item) end
		end
	end
end

-- Client: the go-to order of the stock (kCUSTOM3) or of Useful Idiots (its point key).
local function go_key(dik)
	local mcm = idiots_lib("illish.lib.npc") and _G["ui_mcm"]
	if mcm then
		local key = mcm.get("idiots/keybinds/point/move_key")
		return key ~= nil and key > 0 and key == dik and mcm.get_mod_key(mcm.get("idiots/keybinds/point/move_mod")) and true or false
	end
	return dik_to_bind(dik) == key_bindings.kCUSTOM3
end

local function on_key_press(dik)
	if not (P.client_live() and go_key(dik)) then return end
	local me = P.self_peer()
	for _, peer in pairs(view) do
		if peer == me then
			local pos = level.get_target_pos()
			if pos and P.send(EV_GO, { x = pos.x, y = pos.y, z = pos.z }, 0) then
				actor_menu.set_msg(1, game.translate_string("st_move_to_point"), 8)
			end
			return
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host: run the action for the player, keep the leader, mirror the flags
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function flags_of(npc)
	local t = {}
	for _, flag in ipairs(FLAGS) do
		if npc:has_info(flag) then t[#t + 1] = flag end
	end
	return table.concat(t, ",")
end

local sent_info = {} -- npc id -> peer -> what he was told last
local sent_items = {} -- npc id -> peer -> the list he was sent last

local function members(squad)
	local list = {}
	if not squad then return list end
	for k in squad:squad_members() do
		local st = db.storage[k.id]
		local o = st and st.object or level.object_by_id(k.id)
		if o then list[#list + 1] = o end
	end
	return list
end

-- Who holds control of a companion squad: the peer of its leader, or the host's own: no entry, or a leader out of the world.
local function control_peer(squad)
	local id = leaders[squad.id]
	local peer = id and level.object_by_id(id) and P.peer_of(id)
	if type(peer) == "number" then return peer end
	return P.self_peer()
end

-- Every player learns who holds control (nil: a companion of nobody) and the flags: the dialogs read them on his machine.
local function push_info(npc, leader_peer)
	local id = npc:id()
	sent_info[id] = sent_info[id] or {}
	for _, p in ipairs(P.players()) do
		if not p.is_self then
			local s = leader_peer ~= nil and flags_of(npc) or ""
			local mark = tostring(leader_peer) .. ":" .. s
			if sent_info[id][p.id] ~= mark and P.send(EV_INFO, { i = id, s = s, l = leader_peer }, p.id) then
				sent_info[id][p.id] = mark
				stats.info_out = stats.info_out + 1
			end
		end
	end
end

-- What the group may take back: the stock's list (mode 1: what was given, Useful Idiots adds the loot).
local function push_items(npc)
	local get = axr_companions and axr_companions.get_inventory_table
	if type(get) ~= "function" then return end
	local ids = {}
	for item_id in pairs(get(npc, npc:id(), 1)) do ids[#ids + 1] = item_id end
	table.sort(ids)
	local s = table.concat(ids, ",")
	local id = npc:id()
	sent_items[id] = sent_items[id] or {}
	for _, p in ipairs(P.players()) do
		if not p.is_self and sent_items[id][p.id] ~= s and P.send(EV_ITEMS, { i = id, s = s }, p.id) then
			sent_items[id][p.id] = s
		end
	end
end

local function push_squad(squad, peer)
	for _, o in ipairs(members(squad)) do
		push_info(o, peer)
		push_items(o)
	end
end

local function squad_ids()
	local ids = {}
	local cs = axr_companions and axr_companions.companion_squads
	if type(cs) == "table" then
		for id, sq in pairs(cs) do
			if sq then ids[id] = true end
		end
	end
	return ids
end

-- The squads added since `before` are led by the player. Returns how many. Several for one recruit: Useful Idiots splits a
-- recruited squad into one per member.
local function claim_new_squads(before, peer)
	local who = P.avatar_of_peer(peer)
	local n = 0
	if not who then return n end
	for id in pairs(squad_ids()) do
		if not before[id] then
			leaders[id] = who
			claimed_far(id, who, peer)
			n = n + 1
		end
	end
	return n
end

function squads_now()
	return squad_ids()
end

-- For code that writes the stock table itself (coop_tasks.with_task_owner): the squads added since `before`, that no wrapper claimed, are
-- led by player `peer`. Returns how many.
function claim_since(before, peer)
	local known = {}
	for id in pairs(before) do known[id] = true end
	for id in pairs(squad_ids()) do
		if leaders[id] ~= nil or far_leader(id) ~= nil then known[id] = true end
	end
	return claim_new_squads(known, peer)
end

-- A story lets a companion go and takes it back later, by a line anybody may say (the Fanatic's training): it goes back to who led it. His
-- own "leave me" ends that.
note_let_go = function(squad, dialog_id)
	if not (squad and is_companion_squad(squad)) then return end
	if dialog_id == LEAVE_DIALOG then
		last_leader[squad.id] = nil
	elseif leaders[squad.id] ~= nil then
		last_leader[squad.id] = leaders[squad.id]
	elseif P.is_world_server() then
		last_leader[squad.id] = 0
	end
end

-- The squads added since `before`: he who led one when a story let it go leads it again, if he stands on its level.
give_back = function(before)
	for id in pairs(squad_ids()) do
		local lead = not before[id] and last_leader[id]
		if lead == 0 then
			last_leader[id] = nil
			leaders[id] = nil
		elseif lead then
			last_leader[id] = nil
			if level.object_by_id(lead) and P.peer_of(lead) then leaders[id] = lead end
		end
	end
end

-- Ruling F2-34: did player `from` talk to the NPC, or to a member of its squad, now or in the last RECRUIT_TALK_MS
-- (the host's talk locks, coop.talk_recent)? False without the engine function.
local function talked_recently(from, npc, squad)
	local api = rawget(_G, "coop") or coop
	local recent = api and api.talk_recent
	if type(recent) ~= "function" then return false end
	if recent(from, npc:id(), RECRUIT_TALK_MS) then return true end
	for _, o in ipairs(members(squad)) do
		if recent(from, o:id(), RECRUIT_TALK_MS) then return true end
	end
	return false
end

-- about: a player the message names, whose nick the machine that reads it knows (a map server knows only the players of its level).
local function tell(peer, key, name, nick, about)
	if peer ~= P.self_peer() then
		P.send(EV_MSG, { k = key, n = name, w = nick, a = about }, peer)
	elseif not P.is_map_server() then -- its actor is a ghost, nobody reads it
		show(key, about and nick_of(about) or name, nick)
	end
end

local function host_on_cmd(t, from)
	local full = t.f
	local kind = type(full) == "string" and ACTIONS[full]
	if not kind or type(t.i) ~= "number" then return end
	local npc = level.object_by_id(t.i)
	local who = P.object_of_peer(from)
	if not (npc and npc:alive() and who) then return end
	local m, fn = resolve(full)
	local f = orig[full] or (m and m[fn])
	if type(f) ~= "function" then return end
	local squad = squad_of(npc)
	local leader = squad and leaders[squad.id]
	-- the dialog was face to face; a leader's order reaches his companion from anywhere, as the stock hotkeys (coop_world_compat)
	if leader ~= who:id() and npc:position():distance_to_sqr(who:position()) > FACE_TO_FACE_SQR then
		stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
		return
	end
	-- a companion of the group: everybody's orders, only who holds control dismisses it, and nobody recruits it away (W5)
	if squad and axr_companions and axr_companions.companion_squads[squad.id] then
		if kind == "add" then
			stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
			return
		end
		if kind == "remove" and control_peer(squad) ~= from then
			if t.d == LEAVE_DIALOG then
				stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
				tell(from, "st_coop_comp_refused_not_yours")
				return
			end
			-- a story's line comes out of a talk with it: the dialog's name is a client's word
			if not talked_recently(from, npc, squad) then
				stats.refused_talk = stats.refused_talk + 1
				log("dismissal of %s (%s) by player #%s refused: no talk with it or its squad in the last %d ms", npc:name(),
					tostring(npc:id()), tostring(from), RECRUIT_TALK_MS)
				return
			end
		end
	end
	-- Ruling F2-34: a recruit only right after this player's talk with the NPC or its squad
	if kind == "add" and not talked_recently(from, npc, squad) then
		stats.refused_talk = stats.refused_talk + 1
		log("recruit of %s (%s) by player #%s refused: no talk with it or its squad in the last %d ms", npc:name(),
			tostring(npc:id()), tostring(from), RECRUIT_TALK_MS)
		return
	end
	stats.cmd_in = stats.cmd_in + 1
	if kind == "remove" then note_let_go(squad, t.d) end
	local before = kind == "add" and squad_ids()
	-- (host actor, npc) makes dialogs.who_is_npc pick the NPC. Orders placed at "the actor's" position run
	-- with the client's proxy as db.actor; the rest as stock (they only touch the NPC and its squad).
	if POSITIONAL[full] then
		P.with_identity(who, f, db.actor, npc)
	else
		f(db.actor, npc)
	end
	squad = squad_of(npc)
	if full == PAID then
		local e = squad and txr_paid_companions.paid_companions[squad.id]
		if e then e.guard_period = t.p == PAID_SECONDS.take_guard_money_2 and t.p or PAID_SECONDS.take_guard_money_1 end
	end
	if kind == "add" then
		-- a story's recruit that marks the squad and sets the logic but writes no line of the table (the Fanatic, dialogs_escape): the
		-- stock writes the line from the mark on the next load (squad_on_first_update). A client's recruit needs it now, for a leader.
		local cid = squad and not is_companion_squad(squad) and squad:commander_id()
		local se = cid and alife_object(cid)
		if se and se_load_var(cid, se:name(), "companion") then axr_companions.companion_squads[squad.id] = squad end
		claim_new_squads(before, from)
		give_back(before)
	elseif kind == "remove" and squad then
		leaders[squad.id] = nil
	end
	local peer = is_companion_squad(squad) and control_peer(squad) or nil
	for _, o in ipairs(members(squad)) do push_info(o, peer) end
	if not squad then push_info(npc, nil) end
end

-- Persistent character identity: a disconnected leader's peer slot may already be reused.
function owner_character(npc)
	local squad = npc and squad_of(npc)
	if not squad or not is_companion_squad(squad) then return nil end
	return leaders[squad.id] or 0
end

function leader_of(npc)
	local squad = squad_of(npc)
	local id = squad and leaders[squad.id]
	if not id then return nil end
	local p = level.object_by_id(id)
	if p and P.is_proxy(p) then return p end
	return nil
end

-- Whom this NPC takes for "the actor" on this process: its leader; on a map server, whose actor is a ghost, a companion with no leader
-- here goes to the nearest player of the level. nil: nobody, it runs as it is.
function follows(npc)
	if next(leaders) ~= nil then
		local lead = leader_of(npc)
		if lead then return lead end
	end
	if not P.is_map_server() then return nil end
	local cs = axr_companions and axr_companions.companion_squads
	if type(cs) ~= "table" or next(cs) == nil or not is_companion_squad(squad_of(npc)) then return nil end
	return (P.nearest(npc))
end

-- Ruling F2-32b, the owner's change of 2026-11-01: a companion's inventory is the group's. Asked by the engine for an item move.
function is_group_companion(npc)
	return is_companion_squad(squad_of(npc)) and true or false
end

-- The peer of this squad's leader if he stands on another level than player `peer`.
local function leader_elsewhere(squad, peer)
	local id = leaders[squad.id]
	local lead = 0 -- no entry: the host player's own, on a map server too
	if id then lead = P.peer_of(id) or lead_peer[squad.id] end
	if type(lead) == "number" and lead ~= peer and on_other_level(lead, peer) then return lead end
	return nil
end

-- The host's decision on both commands, for a client's request and for its own dialog alike. act = "take": `from` takes control,
-- "give": `from` hands it to player `to`. Control passes between players of one level (the owner's rule).
local function host_lead(from, act, npc_id, to)
	local function refuse(why, about)
		stats.lead_refused = stats.lead_refused + 1
		log("%s of %s by player #%s refused: %s", tostring(act), tostring(npc_id), tostring(from), why)
		tell(from, "st_coop_comp_refused_" .. why, nil, nil, about)
	end
	local npc = level.object_by_id(npc_id)
	local me = P.object_of_peer(from)
	local squad = npc and npc:alive() and squad_of(npc)
	if not (me and is_companion_squad(squad)) then return refuse("nobody") end
	if npc:position():distance_to_sqr(me:position()) > FACE_TO_FACE_SQR then return refuse("far") end
	local holder = control_peer(squad)
	local target = from
	if act == "give" then
		if holder ~= from then return refuse("not_yours") end
		target = to
		if type(target) ~= "number" or target == from then return refuse("player") end
		if on_other_level(from, target) then return refuse("elsewhere", target) end
	else
		-- before the holder: control_peer says "ours" of a leader out of this process's world
		local away = leader_elsewhere(squad, from)
		if away then return refuse("elsewhere", away) end
		if holder == from then return end -- the same request twice
	end
	local who = P.avatar_of_peer(target)
	if not who then return refuse("player") end
	leaders[squad.id] = target ~= P.self_peer() and who or nil
	stats.lead = stats.lead + 1
	log("squad %s (%s): control %s -> player #%s", tostring(squad.id), npc:name(), tostring(holder), tostring(target))
	push_squad(squad, target)
	local name = npc:character_name()
	if act == "give" then
		tell(from, "st_coop_comp_you_gave", name, nick_of(target))
		tell(target, "st_coop_comp_gave_you", name, nick_of(from))
	else
		tell(from, "st_coop_comp_you_took", name)
		tell(holder, "st_coop_comp_took_from_you", name, nick_of(from))
	end
end

local function host_on_lead(t, from)
	if type(t.i) ~= "number" then return end
	host_lead(from, t.a == "give" and "give" or "take", t.i, t.to)
end

-- A client's Lua state is new: all it knows of the companions came with the save, nothing of it is sure.
local function host_on_req(_, from)
	for _, told in pairs(sent_info) do told[from] = nil end
	for _, told in pairs(sent_items) do told[from] = nil end
	if axr_companions then
		for squad_id in pairs(axr_companions.companion_squads) do
			local squad = alife_object(squad_id)
			if squad then push_squad(squad, control_peer(squad)) end
		end
	end
end

-- A client's item move in his companion's inventory: stock's OnItemAfterMove is host-domain, this is its call for him.
local function host_on_item(t, from)
	if type(t.i) ~= "number" or type(t.o) ~= "number" then return end
	local npc, obj = level.object_by_id(t.i), level.object_by_id(t.o)
	local squad = npc and squad_of(npc)
	if obj and is_companion_squad(squad) and P.object_of_peer(from) then
		axr_companions.OnItemAfterMove(t.i, obj, "loot", t.g == true and EDDListType.iActorBag or EDDListType.iDeadBodyBag)
		push_items(npc)
	end
end

-- A client's go-to: stock move_to_point or Useful Idiots' point key, for the squads he leads.
local function host_on_go(t, from)
	if not (t.x == t.x and t.y == t.y and t.z == t.z and type(t.x) == "number" and type(t.y) == "number" and type(t.z) == "number") then
		return -- a peer's numbers: nan is the one that differs from itself
	end
	local pos = vector():set(t.x, t.y, t.z)
	local NPC = idiots_lib("illish.lib.npc")
	local mcm = NPC and _G["ui_mcm"]
	local wait, guard = mcm and mcm.get("idiots/options/autoWait"), mcm and mcm.get("idiots/options/autoGuard")
	for id in pairs(squad_ids()) do
		local squad = alife_object(id)
		if squad and control_peer(squad) == from and not axr_task_manager.hostages_by_id[squad:commander_id()] then
			for _, o in ipairs(members(squad)) do
				stats.go = stats.go + 1
				if NPC then
					NPC.moveToPoint(o, pos)
					if wait then NPC.setState(o, "movement", "wait", true) end
					if guard then NPC.setState(o, "combat", "guard", true) end
				else
					local lvid = level.vertex_id(pos)
					axr_companions.set_companion_to_follow_state(o)
					save_var(o, "fight_from_point", lvid)
					local st = db.storage[o:id()]
					if st and st.beh and o:id() == squad:commander_id() then st.beh.rally_lvid = lvid end
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

-- Scripted enemies told to walk to "the actor" (target = actor: the mirages, the pump station's attackers, the squads of The Living
-- Fire) go for the nearest player on his feet: the host's character may be down or at a camp across the map. A companion
-- keeps its leader (a squad with no proxy leader is the host's).
local function hunted_player(self)
	if not (self.st and self.st.target == "actor") then return nil end
	local squad = squad_of(self.object)
	local cs = axr_companions and axr_companions.companion_squads
	if squad and type(cs) == "table" and cs[squad.id] ~= nil then return nil end -- false: loaded, no update yet
	local pos = self.object:position()
	local best, best_d
	for _, o in ipairs(P.everyone()) do
		if P.standing(o) then
			local d = o:position():distance_to_sqr(pos)
			if not best_d or d < best_d then best, best_d = o, d end
		end
	end
	return best and P.is_proxy(best) and best or nil
end

local function patch_beh()
	local ab = _G["axr_beh"] and axr_beh.action_beh
	local ex = ab and ab.execute
	if type(ex) ~= "function" or orig.beh then return end
	orig.beh = ex
	ab.execute = function(self, ...)
		if host_on and not P.in_identity() then
			-- this target reads a var of the actor, which a proxy has not (axr_beh set_desired_target)
			local anomaly = self.st and self.st.target == "task_target_anomaly"
			local lead = not anomaly and (follows(self.object) or hunted_player(self))
			if lead then
				stats.follow = stats.follow + 1
				return P.with_identity(lead, ex, self, ...)
			end
		end
		return ex(self, ...)
	end
end

-- The leader of this companion for stock code outside axr_beh; nil: run it as it is.
local function lead_for(npc)
	if host_on and not P.in_identity() then return follows(npc) end
	return nil
end

refuse_dismiss = function(npc, dialog_id)
	if dialog_id ~= LEAVE_DIALOG or not lead_for(npc) then return false end
	stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
	tell(P.self_peer(), "st_coop_comp_refused_not_yours")
	return true
end

local function run_as_leader(cls, name)
	local f = cls and cls[name]
	if type(f) ~= "function" then return end
	cls[name] = function(self, ...)
		local lead = lead_for(self.object)
		if lead then return P.with_identity(lead, f, self, ...) end
		return f(self, ...)
	end
end

-- Stock code over every companion squad, for the host's own keys, wheel and squad list: it sees the squads he leads.
local function own_squads_only(ac, name)
	local f = ac[name]
	if type(f) ~= "function" then return end
	ac[name] = function(...)
		if not (host_on and (next(leaders) ~= nil or next(far) ~= nil)) then return f(...) end
		local all, own = ac.companion_squads, {}
		for id, squad in pairs(all) do
			if not squad or (control_peer(squad) == P.self_peer() and not far_leader(id)) then own[id] = squad end
		end
		ac.companion_squads = own
		local res = { pcall(f, ...) }
		ac.companion_squads = all
		if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
		return unpack(res, 2)
	end
end

-- Is this companion led by the player the code runs for: the one under with_identity, else the host?
local function led_here(npc)
	local lead = follows(npc)
	if P.in_identity() then return lead ~= nil and lead:id() == db.actor:id() end
	return lead == nil
end

-- Useful Idiots keeps "the companions" in one list. Its formations, the panel and the keys want those of one player; its surge
-- rules protect or expose every companion alike.
local function patch_idiots(NPC)
	local get, target = NPC.getCompanions, NPC.getTargetCompanion
	NPC.getCompanions = function()
		if P.client_live() then -- the wheel opened only on a companion under the cursor: getTargetCompanion reads the NPC's flag
			local own = {}
			for _, id in ipairs(client_own_ids()) do
				local npc = level.object_by_id(id)
				if npc and npc:alive() then own[#own + 1] = npc end
			end
			return own
		end
		local list = get()
		if not (host_on and next(leaders) ~= nil) or every_companion > 0 then return list end
		local own = {}
		for _, npc in ipairs(list) do
			if led_here(npc) then own[#own + 1] = npc end
		end
		return own
	end
	NPC.getTargetCompanion = function(...)
		local npc = target(...)
		if npc and lead_for(npc) then return nil end
		return npc
	end
	local surge = idiots_lib("illish.patches.surge_manager")
	for _, name in ipairs({ "obfuscateCompanions", "addCompanionStoryIds", "removeCompanionStoryIds" }) do
		local f = surge and surge[name]
		if type(f) == "function" then
			surge[name] = function()
				every_companion = every_companion + 1
				local ok, err = pcall(f)
				every_companion = every_companion - 1
				if not ok then error(err, 0) end
			end
		end
	end
	for _, name in ipairs({ "assault", "guard", "snipe", "support" }) do
		local m = _G["idiots_combat_" .. name]
		local cls = m and m["action_combat_" .. name]
		run_as_leader(cls, "initialize")
		run_as_leader(cls, "execute")
	end
end

-- "He is with me" and its Useful Idiots replacement: no fight between a companion and whoever is no enemy of "the actor".
local function patch_enemy_rule()
	local ignore, with_me = idiots_lib("illish.patches.xr_combat_ignore"), _G["he_is_with_me"]
	local f = ignore and ignore.onEvalEnemy or with_me and with_me.escorteval
	if type(f) ~= "function" then return end
	local function eval(npc, enemy, flags)
		local lead = lead_for(npc) or lead_for(enemy)
		if lead then return P.with_identity(lead, f, npc, enemy, flags) end
		return f(npc, enemy, flags)
	end
	if ignore and ignore.onEvalEnemy then ignore.onEvalEnemy = eval end
	if with_me and with_me.escorteval == f then with_me.escorteval = eval end
end

local function patch_leader_paths()
	local ac = axr_companions
	if ac then
		for _, name in ipairs({ "cycle_state", "move_to_point", "list_actor_squad_by_id", "get_nearby_companion" }) do
			own_squads_only(ac, name)
		end
		local list = ac.list_actor_squad_by_id
		if type(list) == "function" then
			ac.list_actor_squad_by_id = function(...) -- the stock's panel, the PDA's relations tab: a client's own companions
				if P.client_live() then return client_own_ids() end
				return list(...)
			end
		end
		local nearby = ac.get_nearby_companion
		if type(nearby) == "function" then
			ac.get_nearby_companion = function() -- the stock asks the flag of the NPC under the cursor first
				local res = nearby()
				if res and res ~= true and lead_for(res) then return #ac.list_actor_squad_by_id() > 0 end
				return res
			end
		end
	end
	local m = _G["sim_squad_scripted"]
	local cls = m and m.sim_squad_scripted
	local task = cls and cls.get_current_task
	if type(task) == "function" then
		cls.get_current_task = function(self)
			local id = host_on and self.assigned_target_id == 0 and leaders[self.id] -- 0: the stock's "actor"
			local lead = id and level.object_by_id(id)
			if lead and P.peer_of(id) then return CALifeSmartTerrainTask(lead:game_vertex_id(), lead:level_vertex_id()) end
			return task(self)
		end
	end
	-- stock code that brings a companion squad to "the actor" by hand (an offline spy, tasks_agent_rescue)
	local teleport = rawget(_G, "TeleportSquad")
	if type(teleport) == "function" then
		_G.TeleportSquad = function(squad, pos, lvid, gvid)
			local id = host_on and squad and leaders[squad.id]
			local lead = id and level.object_by_id(id)
			if lead and P.peer_of(id) and pos:distance_to_sqr(db.actor:position()) < 1 then
				return teleport(squad, lead:position(), lead:level_vertex_id(), lead:game_vertex_id())
			end
			return teleport(squad, pos, lvid, gvid)
		end
	end
	local NPC = idiots_lib("illish.lib.npc")
	if NPC then patch_idiots(NPC) end
	patch_enemy_rule()
end

-- A companion's logic starts a talk with "the actor" (beh_companion.ltx: the ecologists' talk at the destination): his leader's machine
-- opens it. The stock runs it on this process's actor, a host who may not be near, a ghost on a map server.
local function patch_force_talk()
	local fx = _G["xr_effects"]
	local f = fx and fx.force_talk
	if type(f) ~= "function" or orig.force_talk then return end
	orig.force_talk = f
	fx.force_talk = function(actor, npc, p)
		local lead = host_on and npc and follows(npc)
		local peer = lead and P.peer_of(lead)
		if type(peer) == "number" then
			P.send(EV_TALK, { i = npc:id(), b = p and p[1] == "true" or false }, peer)
			return
		end
		if not P.is_map_server() then return f(actor, npc, p) end
	end
end

local function client_on_talk(t)
	local npc = type(t.i) == "number" and level.object_by_id(P.to_local(t.i))
	if npc and db.actor then db.actor:run_talk_dialog(npc, t.b == true) end
end

-- Companions a task gives (on_init of the escort, raid and hostage tasks, Mystery of the Swamps, the speaker of
-- simulation_task_66/67) join the player the task was taken by, not the host. While coop_tasks gives a task for a client
-- (reward_peer), every squad one of these calls adds to companion_squads is led by that player's proxy, like a dialog
-- recruit: axr_beh then follows him.
-- (axr_companions first: loading it defines its xr_effects, which are looked up after it)
local TASK_SQUADS = {
	{ "axr_companions", "add_special_squad" }, { "nta_utils", "spawn_companion_squad" },
	{ "xr_effects", "setup_companion_task" }, { "xr_effects", "add_task_companion" },
	{ "xr_effects", "add_speaker_companion" },
}

local function task_taker()
	local ct = rawget(_G, "coop_tasks")
	local peer = ct and type(ct.reward_peer) == "function" and ct.reward_peer()
	return type(peer) == "number" and peer or nil
end

-- The speaker of add_speaker_companion is the NPC the host's player talks to; the host is not talking while a client
-- takes the task, so the giver stands in for the talk for this one call.
local function as_speaker(giver, f, ...)
	local mt = rawget(_G, "mob_trade")
	local talking = mt and mt.GetTalkingNpc
	if mt then mt.GetTalkingNpc = function() return giver end end
	local a = db.actor
	local is_talking = a.is_talking
	a.is_talking = function() return true end
	local res = { pcall(f, ...) }
	a.is_talking = is_talking
	if mt then mt.GetTalkingNpc = talking end
	if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
	return unpack(res, 2)
end

local function wrap_task_squads()
	for _, t in ipairs(TASK_SQUADS) do
		local key = t[1] .. "." .. t[2]
		local okm, m = pcall(function() return _G[t[1]] end)
		local f = okm and type(m) == "table" and m[t[2]]
		if type(f) == "function" and not orig[key] then
			orig[key] = f
			m[t[2]] = function(...)
				local peer = installed and task_taker()
				if not peer then return f(...) end
				local before = squad_ids()
				local res
				local ct = rawget(_G, "coop_tasks")
				local giver = t[2] == "add_speaker_companion" and ct and type(ct.giving_npc) == "function" and ct.giving_npc()
				if giver and not db.actor:is_talking() then
					res = { pcall(as_speaker, giver, f, ...) }
				else
					res = { pcall(f, ...) }
				end
				if res[1] and t[2] == "add_special_squad" then mark_far(before, ...) end
				stats.task_squads = stats.task_squads + claim_new_squads(before, peer)
				if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
				return unpack(res, 2)
			end
		end
	end
end

-- The stock's marks of a member, written as the stock writes them on one it holds.
local function put_marks(id, companion, cannot_dismiss, cannot_teleport)
	local se = alife_object(id)
	if not se then return end
	local name = se:name()
	se_save_var(id, name, "companion", companion)
	se_save_var(id, name, "companion_cannot_dismiss", cannot_dismiss)
	se_save_var(id, name, "companion_cannot_teleport", cannot_teleport)
end

-- The stock's marks of a squad, as the binder of its members reads them when they come online.
local function marks_of(squad)
	local id = squad:commander_id()
	local se = id and alife_object(id)
	if not se then return {} end
	local name = se:name()
	return { m = se_load_var(id, name, "companion") and true or nil, d = se_load_var(id, name, "companion_cannot_dismiss") and true or nil,
		c = se_load_var(id, name, "companion_cannot_teleport") and true or nil }
end

-- A save holds the leaders of every level: once after a load, a squad of another level is its authority's. The world server keeps the
-- word for the next save, a map server drops it. Once: a squad a map server adopts later stands, on its copy of the world, where it last
-- heard of it (the place comes after the word).
local function keep_own_level()
	if not sort_due then return end
	sort_due = false
	if not split_levels() then return end
	for squad_id, lead in pairs(leaders) do
		local squad = alife_object(squad_id)
		local level_id, at = nil, nil
		if squad then level_id, at = level_of_squad(squad) end
		if at and at ~= level.name() then
			leaders[squad_id] = nil
			if P.is_world_server() then note_far(level_id, squad_id, lead) end
		end
	end
end

local function host_refresh()
	if not axr_companions then return end
	keep_own_level()
	local cs = axr_companions.companion_squads
	local live = {}
	for squad_id in pairs(cs) do
		local squad = alife_object(squad_id)
		if squad then
			for k in squad:squad_members() do live[k.id] = true end
			push_squad(squad, control_peer(squad))
		end
	end
	for squad_id in pairs(leaders) do
		local squad = alife_object(squad_id)
		-- recruited on a map server the table of the save has no line of it, the stock's mark on its members stays (the binder reads it)
		if squad and cs[squad_id] == nil and marks_of(squad).m then cs[squad_id] = squad end
		if cs[squad_id] == nil or not squad then -- a loaded squad is false until its first update
			leaders[squad_id] = nil -- dismissed by the host, dead or released
		end
	end
	for _, row in pairs(far) do
		for squad_id in pairs(row) do
			if not alife_object(squad_id) then row[squad_id] = nil end
		end
	end
	for squad_id in pairs(last_leader) do
		if not alife_object(squad_id) then last_leader[squad_id] = nil end
	end
	-- the last word about whom this was: a contract's end, a dismissal by the host, a death
	for id, told in pairs(sent_info) do
		if not live[id] then
			for peer in pairs(told) do P.send(EV_INFO, { i = id, s = "" }, peer) end
			sent_info[id], sent_items[id] = nil, nil
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A leader on another level (split levels, one player moves): his companions go after him. The authority of the level he left lets
-- them go; the world server teleports them when none of them is online at a map server, and tells the authority of his level.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local followers = {} -- world server: squad id -> { p = peer, l = leader's character, b = bridge of the map server that let it go }
-- map server: squad id -> true: let go to the world server, still here and still its owner's until the world server took it (npc.comp_drop
-- with m): a friend who stays by it keeps it online here, and nothing may forget whose it is meanwhile
local leaving = {}
local adopting = {} -- map server: squad id -> { word of the world server, when it came }: the squad is not here yet
local ADOPT_WAIT_MS = 60000

-- This process takes the squad. t: the world server's word with the stock's marks, it writes them for a map server's copy of the world.
local function adopt(squad_id, lead, t)
	local squad = alife_object(squad_id)
	if not (squad and axr_companions) then return false end
	leaders[squad_id] = lead
	axr_companions.companion_squads[squad_id] = squad
	lead_peer[squad_id] = t and t.p or lead_peer[squad_id]
	for k in squad:squad_members() do
		if t then put_marks(k.id, true, t.d or nil, t.c or nil) end
		local st = db.storage[k.id]
		local npc = st and st.object or level.object_by_id(k.id)
		if npc and not npc:has_info("npcx_is_companion") then -- a second setup would reset his orders
			axr_companions.setup_companion_logic(npc, st, false, t and t.d)
		end
	end
	return true
end

-- World server: the map server of the level this squad stands on, and that level's id.
local function map_server_of(squad)
	local l = split_levels()
	if not (l and P.is_world_server()) then return nil end
	local id = level_of_squad(squad)
	for _, ms in ipairs(l.map_servers()) do
		if ms.level == id then return ms.bridge, id end
	end
	return nil
end

local function send_adopt(bridge, squad, lead, peer)
	local m = marks_of(squad)
	return P.send(EV_ADOPT, { s = squad.id, l = lead, p = peer, d = m.d, c = m.c }, bridge)
end

-- World server: a squad that was just claimed and stands on a map server's level is that server's to lead.
claimed_far = function(squad_id, lead, peer)
	local squad = alife_object(squad_id)
	if not squad then return end
	local bridge, level_id = map_server_of(squad)
	if not bridge then return end
	leaders[squad_id] = nil
	note_far(level_id, squad_id, lead)
	send_adopt(bridge, squad, lead, peer)
end

-- The stock's add_special_squad marks a member only where he is a live NPC, and the world server has none of a map server's level: the
-- escort would come with no ban on dismissing it. The marks go on its record: the word to the map server reads them there, the next word
-- (follow_home) and the save too. Called with the arguments of the stock function.
mark_far = function(before, squad, special, cannot_teleport)
	if not squad or before[squad.id] or not map_server_of(squad) then return end
	for k in squad:squad_members() do put_marks(k.id, true, true, cannot_teleport and true or nil) end
end

local function all_home(squad, l)
	for k in squad:squad_members() do
		if l.online_at_server(k.id) then return false end
	end
	return true
end

-- May this squad go after its leader? Stock's rule (Useful Idiots' over it): not one told to wait, not one that cannot teleport.
local function may_follow(squad)
	local ac = axr_companions
	local f = orig.can_teleport or (ac and ac.companion_squad_can_teleport)
	return type(f) ~= "function" or f(squad) == true
end

-- World server: a friend who stays by the squad keeps it online at its map server, and it would never come home. That server is asked to
-- take it offline now and give it back (coop.levels.recall there), once, and again only after a while: the word or its answer can be lost.
-- Never a squad that may not teleport: it stays where it is, as in the stock. An engine without holder_of: it waits, as before.
local function ask_recall(l, squad_id, squad, f)
	if not l.holder_of or (f.r and time_global() - f.r < RECALL_AGAIN_MS) or not may_follow(squad) then return end
	local bridge = l.holder_of(squad_id)
	for k in squad:squad_members() do bridge = bridge or l.holder_of(k.id) end
	if bridge and P.send(EV_RECALL, { s = squad_id }, bridge) then
		f.r = time_global()
		stats.recall = stats.recall + 1
		log("recall of squad %s asked of map server %s", tostring(squad_id), tostring(bridge))
	end
end

local function follow_home(l)
	for squad_id, f in pairs(followers) do
		local squad = alife_object(squad_id)
		local _, at = nil, nil
		if squad then _, at = level_of_squad(squad) end
		if not squad then
			followers[squad_id] = nil
		elseif at and at == l.level_name(l.level_of_player(f.p)) then
			followers[squad_id] = nil -- he came back before it left: the map server there leads it again (follow_tick)
		elseif all_home(squad, l) then
			local body = nil
			for _, p in ipairs(P.players()) do
				if p.id == f.p then body = p.avatar_id and alife_object(p.avatar_id) end
			end
			if body then
				TeleportSquad(squad, body.position, body.m_level_vertex_id, body.m_game_vertex_id)
				followers[squad_id] = nil
				stats.follow = stats.follow + 1
				if f.b then P.send(EV_DROP, { s = squad_id, m = true }, f.b) end -- the map server it left forgets it, no dismissal
				local bridge = l.bridge_of_player(f.p)
				if bridge then
					axr_companions.companion_squads[squad_id] = nil
					note_far(l.level_of_player(f.p), squad_id, f.l)
					send_adopt(bridge, squad, f.l, f.p)
				else
					note_far(nil, squad_id)
					adopt(squad_id, f.l)
				end
			end
		else
			ask_recall(l, squad_id, squad, f)
		end
	end
end

-- World server: it stands in for the authority of a level nobody leads. A level entered together leaves a squad somebody else leads behind
-- (teleport_rule) while its leader comes along: the squad goes after him as any other. Every tick and not with the sort of the save: a
-- character is back in the list of players a moment after the world. Its word stays in `far` until it is taken: the save needs it.
local function left_behind(l)
	local led = {}
	for _, ms in ipairs(l.map_servers()) do led[ms.level] = true end
	for level_id, row in pairs(far) do
		if not led[level_id] then
			for squad_id, lead in pairs(row) do
				local squad = alife_object(squad_id)
				local peer = P.peer_of(lead)
				local there = peer and l.level_name(l.level_of_player(peer))
				if squad and there and not followers[squad_id] then
					local _, at = level_of_squad(squad)
					if at and there ~= at and may_follow(squad) then followers[squad_id] = { p = peer, l = lead } end
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

local function follow_tick()
	local l = split_levels()
	if not l then return end
	for squad_id, lead in pairs(leaders) do
		local peer = P.peer_of(lead) or lead_peer[squad_id]
		lead_peer[squad_id] = peer
		local there = peer and l.level_name(l.level_of_player(peer))
		local squad = alife_object(squad_id)
		if leaving[squad_id] then
			if there == level.name() then -- he came back first: the world server drops its way too
				if leaving[squad_id] == RECALLED and l.recall then l.recall(squad_id, 0) end -- it may come online for him at once
				leaving[squad_id] = nil
			end
		elseif there and there ~= level.name() and (not squad or may_follow(squad)) then
			if P.is_map_server() then
				-- the squad goes when the engine gives it back (nothing of it online here); a friend by it keeps it here, so the owner stays
				leaving[squad_id] = P.send(EV_FOLLOW, { s = squad_id, p = peer, l = lead }, 0) or nil
			else
				leaders[squad_id], lead_peer[squad_id] = nil, nil
				followers[squad_id] = { p = peer, l = lead }
			end
		end
	end
	if P.is_world_server() then
		left_behind(l)
		follow_home(l)
	end
end

-- The stock's level change takes every companion along; with split levels a squad somebody else leads stays where it is. Useful Idiots
-- replaces this function after this script's on_game_start (z_idiots_patches): the wrapper goes on in the update, and again over a later
-- patch. follow_tick asks what was there before: the leader's own going is not the host's.
local function wrap_teleport()
	local ac = axr_companions
	local f = ac and ac.companion_squad_can_teleport
	if type(f) ~= "function" or f == teleport_rule then return end
	orig.can_teleport = f
	teleport_rule = function(squad)
		if squad and split_levels() and (leaders[squad.id] ~= nil or far_leader(squad.id) ~= nil) then return false end
		return f(squad)
	end
	ac.companion_squad_can_teleport = teleport_rule
end

-- Map server: the word that came before its squad.
local function adopt_tick()
	local now = time_global()
	for squad_id, a in pairs(adopting) do
		if adopt(squad_id, a.t.l, a.t) or now - a.at > ADOPT_WAIT_MS then adopting[squad_id] = nil end
	end
end

local function on_follow(t, from)
	if P.is_world_server() and from >= 0x100 and type(t.s) == "number" and type(t.p) == "number" then
		followers[t.s] = { p = t.p, l = t.l, b = from }
		note_far(nil, t.s)
	end
end

local function on_adopt(t, from)
	if not (P.is_map_server() and from == 0 and type(t.s) == "number" and type(t.l) == "number") then return end
	if not adopt(t.s, t.l, t) then adopting[t.s] = { t = t, at = time_global() } end
end

-- A task of the world server lets a squad go that a map server holds (Hidden Threat, the player left the station): the NPC is there.
local function on_drop(t, from)
	if not (P.is_map_server() and from == 0 and type(t.s) == "number") then return end
	local recalled = leaving[t.s] == RECALLED
	leaders[t.s], adopting[t.s], lead_peer[t.s], leaving[t.s] = nil, nil, nil, nil
	if t.m == true then -- m: it went to its leader on another level, the world server took it; no dismissal
		if axr_companions then axr_companions.companion_squads[t.s] = nil end
		local l = recalled and split_levels()
		if l and l.recall then l.recall(t.s, 0) end -- it is on his level now: the pin has nothing left to hold
		return
	end
	local squad = alife_object(t.s)
	if squad and is_companion_squad(squad) then axr_companions.dismiss_special_squad(squad) end
end

-- Map server: the world server's word (npc.comp_recall). Only a squad this server let go itself and that may still teleport; a client's
-- word comes with his peer, never 0 (coop_script.cpp server_on_script_event), and the engine's recall is a map server's alone.
local function on_recall(t, from)
	local l = split_levels()
	if not (l and l.recall and P.is_map_server() and from == 0 and type(t.s) == "number" and leaving[t.s]) then return end
	local squad = alife_object(t.s)
	if squad and may_follow(squad) and l.recall(t.s) then
		leaving[t.s] = RECALLED
		stats.recall = stats.recall + 1
		log("squad %s recalled by the world server: offline here until it took it", tostring(t.s))
	end
end

local function patch_dismiss()
	local ac = axr_companions
	local f = ac and ac.dismiss_special_squad
	if type(f) ~= "function" or orig.dismiss then return end
	orig.dismiss = f
	ac.dismiss_special_squad = function(squad)
		local way = squad and followers[squad.id]
		local bridge = squad and (far_leader(squad.id) and map_server_of(squad) or way and way.b)
		f(squad)
		if not squad then return end
		note_far(nil, squad.id)
		leaders[squad.id], lead_peer[squad.id], followers[squad.id], leaving[squad.id] = nil, nil, nil, nil
		-- the stock takes the marks off the members online here: those of the others would make it a companion again (host_refresh, the binder)
		for k in squad:squad_members() do put_marks(k.id, nil, nil, nil) end
		if bridge then P.send(EV_DROP, { s = squad.id }, bridge) end
	end
end

-- Who leads what, between the processes (coop_levels_share): the squads of a map server's level are its own, the save is the world
-- server's. Up: what this map server leads. Down: all of it, a new map server takes the squads of its level, once: what it changed
-- after that is newer than what the world server has heard.
local function leaders_here()
	if sort_due then return nil end -- the leaders of a save are every level's: this word would take them off the rows of the other map servers
	local t = {}
	-- not one on its way out: the world server holds its owner (followers), this word would put it back on this level's row
	for id, lead in pairs(leaders) do t[id] = not leaving[id] and lead or nil end
	for id, a in pairs(adopting) do t[id] = a.t.l end
	return { l = t, b = last_leader }
end

local function leaders_heard(v, level_id)
	if type(v) ~= "table" or type(v.l) ~= "table" or level_id == nil then return end
	for id in pairs(v.l) do note_far(nil, id) end
	far[level_id] = v.l
	far_last[level_id] = type(v.b) == "table" and v.b or nil
end

local function all_leaders()
	local t, peers = {}, {}
	for id, lead in pairs(leaders) do t[id] = lead end
	for _, row in pairs(far) do
		for id, lead in pairs(row) do t[id] = lead end
	end
	-- on its way to its leader: on_follow took it off `far`; after a load the authority of its level lets it go again (follow_tick)
	for id, f in pairs(followers) do t[id] = f.l end
	for _, p in ipairs(P.players()) do
		if type(p.avatar_id) == "number" then peers[p.avatar_id] = p.id end
	end
	return { l = t, p = peers }
end

local function leaders_given(v)
	if down_heard or type(v) ~= "table" or type(v.l) ~= "table" then return end
	down_heard = true
	local peers = type(v.p) == "table" and v.p or {}
	for id, lead in pairs(v.l) do
		local squad = type(id) == "number" and alife_object(id)
		local at = nil
		if squad then
			local _
			_, at = level_of_squad(squad)
		end
		if at == level.name() then
			if leaders[id] == nil then adopt(id, lead) end
			-- also for a leader of the save: this session may never have seen him, and follow_tick asks where he stands
			if leaders[id] == lead then lead_peer[id] = peers[lead] or lead_peer[id] end
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The commands of the companion's dialog (the machine of the player who talks)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Who holds control of this NPC, as this machine knows it; nil: a companion of nobody.
local function holder_of(npc)
	if P.is_host() then
		local squad = squad_of(npc)
		return is_companion_squad(squad) and control_peer(squad) or nil
	end
	return view[npc:id()]
end

-- The engine's functor<bool> dies on an error or on anything but a boolean.
local function answer(f, ...)
	local ok, res = pcall(f, ...)
	if not ok then report("dialog", res) end
	return ok and res == true
end

-- This player leads this NPC's squad: a hotkey is for his own, it should not reach a friend's.
function held_here(npc)
	return holder_of(npc) == P.self_peer()
end

local function just_asked(npc)
	local at = asked_lead[npc:id()]
	return at ~= nil and time_global() - at < TAKE_WAIT_MS
end

local function may_hand(a, b)
	local npc = npc_of(a, b)
	return P.active() and holder_of(npc) == P.self_peer() and #other_players() > 0 and not just_asked(npc)
end

local function may_take(a, b)
	local npc = npc_of(a, b)
	local peer = holder_of(npc)
	return P.active() and peer ~= nil and peer ~= P.self_peer() and not just_asked(npc)
end

local function slot_player(params)
	return other_players()[tonumber(params and params[1]) or 0]
end

local function ask_lead(act, npc, to)
	asked_lead[npc:id()] = time_global()
	if P.client_live() then
		P.send(EV_LEAD, { a = act, i = P.to_host(npc:id()), to = to }, 0)
	else
		host_lead(P.self_peer(), act, npc:id(), to)
	end
end

function dlg_can_hand(a, b) return answer(may_hand, a, b) end
function dlg_can_take(a, b) return answer(may_take, a, b) end
function dlg_slot(a, b, dialog_id, phrase_id, next_id, params) return answer(function() return slot_player(params) ~= nil end) end

-- The line of a player: his nick, and where he stands if he is out of reach: the host would refuse.
local function slot_text(params)
	local p = slot_player(params)
	if not p then return "" end
	if p.elsewhere == true then return string.format(game.translate_string("st_coop_comp_refused_elsewhere"), tostring(p.nick)) end
	return tostring(p.nick)
end

function dlg_slot_text(a, b, dialog_id, phrase_id, next_id, params)
	local ok, text = pcall(slot_text, params)
	return ok and text or ""
end

function dlg_hand(a, b, dialog_id, phrase_id, next_id, params)
	local ok, err = pcall(function()
		local p = slot_player(params)
		if p then ask_lead("give", npc_of(a, b), p.id) end
	end)
	if not ok then report("hand over", err) end
end

function dlg_take(a, b)
	local ok, err = pcall(ask_lead, "take", npc_of(a, b))
	if not ok then report("take control", err) end
end

-- The lines go into the list of commands of dm_is_actor_companion_dialog (phrase 1 of the stock's init_func), or, top = true, make a
-- dialog of their own (dm_coop_companion_hand: a character with no such list). Conditions with a (n) come to the function in its params
-- table, as a string (engine: DIALOG_UPGRADE); add_dialog of the stock refuses such names.
local function add_lead_phrases(dialog, top)
	local function add(id, prev, text)
		local phrase = dialog:AddPhrase(text, tostring(id), tostring(prev), PHRASE_GOODWILL)
		return phrase and phrase:GetPhraseScript()
	end
	local first = top and 0 or PHRASE_HAND
	local script = add(first, top and "" or 1, "st_coop_comp_cmd_hand")
	if not script then return end
	script:AddPrecondition("coop_npc_companions.dlg_can_hand")
	add(PHRASE_WHOM, first, "st_coop_comp_cmd_whom")
	for slot = 1, OTHER_PLAYERS do
		script = add(PHRASE_SLOTS + slot, PHRASE_WHOM, "st_coop_comp_cmd_hand")
		script:AddPrecondition("coop_npc_companions.dlg_slot(" .. slot .. ")")
		script:SetScriptText("coop_npc_companions.dlg_slot_text(" .. slot .. ")")
		script:AddAction("coop_npc_companions.dlg_hand(" .. slot .. ")")
	end
	add(PHRASE_BACK, PHRASE_WHOM, "axr_phrase_actor_give_command_nevermind") -- the engine asserts on a list with no line
end

-- init_func of dm_coop_companion_hand (modxml_coop_companions).
function dm_init_hand(dialog)
	local ok, err = pcall(add_lead_phrases, dialog, true)
	if not ok then report("hand-over dialog", err) end
end

local function patch_dialog()
	local d = _G["dialogs_axr_companion"]
	if not d then return end
	local init, is_not = d.dm_init_is_actor_companion, d.is_not_actor_companion
	if type(init) == "function" then
		d.dm_init_is_actor_companion = function(dialog)
			init(dialog)
			local ok, err = pcall(add_lead_phrases, dialog) -- the stock list must stand, whatever happens to ours
			if not ok then report("lines of the list of commands", err) end
		end
	end
	-- no offer to recruit a companion of the group
	if type(is_not) == "function" then
		d.is_not_actor_companion = function(a, b, ...)
			local res = is_not(a, b, ...)
			local npc = npc_of(a, b)
			if res and npc and view[npc:id()] ~= nil then return false end
			return res
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Install, update, events, save
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local next_tick, next_refresh = 0, 0

local function actor_on_update()
	local now = time_global()
	if now < next_tick then return end
	next_tick = now + 250
	host_on = installed and P.host_with_clients()
	wrap_teleport()
	-- a map server goes on with nobody left: a leader who just went is off its list of players, and his squad has to go after him
	if (host_on or (installed and P.is_map_server() and split_levels() ~= nil)) and now >= next_refresh then
		next_refresh = now + 2000
		local ok, err = pcall(host_refresh)
		if not ok then report("refresh", err) end
		ok, err = pcall(follow_tick)
		if not ok then report("follow", err) end
		ok, err = pcall(adopt_tick)
		if not ok then report("adopt", err) end
	end
	if not host_on then sent_info, sent_items = {}, {} end
	if P.client_live() then
		if not asked then asked = P.send(EV_REQ, {}, 0) end
		for id, flags in pairs(waiting_flags) do
			local npc = level.object_by_id(id)
			if npc then
				waiting_flags[id] = nil
				apply_flags(npc, flags)
			end
		end
	end
end

local function save_state(m_data)
	local t = all_leaders().l
	m_data.coop_npc_leaders = next(t) ~= nil and t or nil
	local gone = {}
	for id, lead in pairs(last_leader) do gone[id] = lead end
	for _, row in pairs(far_last) do
		for id, lead in pairs(row) do gone[id] = lead end
	end
	m_data.coop_npc_last_leaders = next(gone) ~= nil and gone or nil
end

local function load_state(m_data)
	leaders = {}
	sort_due = true
	far = {}
	followers, leaving = {}, {} -- a way of the old world: the leaders of the save start it again (follow_tick)
	last_leader = {}
	far_last = {}
	if type(m_data.coop_npc_last_leaders) == "table" then
		for k, v in pairs(m_data.coop_npc_last_leaders) do
			if type(k) == "number" and type(v) == "number" then last_leader[k] = v end
		end
	end
	if type(m_data.coop_npc_leaders) == "table" then
		for k, v in pairs(m_data.coop_npc_leaders) do
			if type(k) == "number" and type(v) == "number" then leaders[k] = v end
		end
	end
end

function print_status()
	local n = 0
	for _ in pairs(leaders) do n = n + 1 end
	log("installed %s | squads led by clients %d | orders out %d in %d refused %d, recruits without a talk %d | flags out %d in %d | follow ticks %d, recalls %d | control changed %d refused %d | go-to %d | errors %d",
		tostring(installed), n, stats.cmd_out, stats.cmd_in, stats.refused, stats.refused_talk, stats.info_out, stats.info_in,
		stats.follow, stats.recall, stats.lead, stats.lead_refused, stats.go, P.error_count(TAG))
end

function on_game_start()
	P = coop_npc_players
	if not rawget(_G, "coop") then return end
	if not installed then
		for _, s in ipairs({ { "client actions", patch_client_actions }, { "beh", patch_beh },
			{ "task squads", wrap_task_squads }, { "leader paths", patch_leader_paths }, { "force talk", patch_force_talk }, { "dialog", patch_dialog },
			{ "items", patch_items }, { "dismiss", patch_dismiss } }) do
			local ok, err = pcall(s[2])
			if not ok then report("install " .. s[1], err) end
		end
		installed = true
	end
	P.on(EV_CMD, host_on_cmd, "host", TAG)
	P.on(EV_INFO, client_on_info, "client", TAG)
	P.on(EV_LEAD, host_on_lead, "host", TAG)
	P.on(EV_REQ, host_on_req, "host", TAG)
	P.on(EV_GO, host_on_go, "host", TAG)
	P.on(EV_ITEM, host_on_item, "host", TAG)
	P.on(EV_MSG, client_on_msg, "client", TAG)
	P.on(EV_ITEMS, client_on_items, "client", TAG)
	P.on(EV_TALK, client_on_talk, "client", TAG)
	P.on(EV_FOLLOW, on_follow, nil, TAG)
	P.on(EV_ADOPT, on_adopt, nil, TAG)
	P.on(EV_DROP, on_drop, nil, TAG)
	P.on(EV_RECALL, on_recall, nil, TAG)
	local share = rawget(_G, "coop_levels_share") or coop_levels_share
	if share then
		share.up("comp_leaders", leaders_here, leaders_heard)
		share.down("comp_leaders", all_leaders, leaders_given)
	end
	RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_update", actor_on_update)
	RegisterScriptCallback("on_key_press", on_key_press)
	RegisterScriptCallback("ActorMenu_on_item_after_move", on_item_after_move)
	RegisterScriptCallback("save_state", save_state)
	RegisterScriptCallback("load_state", load_state)
end

function _set_host_on(v) host_on = v end
function _follow_tick() follow_tick() end
function _leaders() return leaders end
function _stats() return stats end
